31, 2026, net cash used in operating activities was $4,017,456, as compared to net cash used in operating activities of $2,345,333 for
the year ended March 31, 2025, representing an increase in cash outflow of $1,672,123. The increase in cash outflow in operating activities
primarily resulted from the change of the following accounts:</p><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&#160;</p><table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse">
<tbody><tr style="vertical-align: top">
<td style="width: 48px; text-align: justify">&#160;</td>
<td style="width: 24px; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">a)</span></td>
<td style="text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">A net loss for the year
    ended March 31, 2026 of $6,205,085, compared with a net loss of $3,303,652 for the year ended March 31, 2025. Excluding the adjustments
    of non-cash items, net loss for the year ended March 31, 2026 and 2025 were $1,627,272 and $1,373,598, respectively. This represents
    a increase in cash outflow of $253,674 for the year ended March 31, 2026, compared with the year ended March 31, 2025.</span></td></tr>
</tbody></table><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&#160;</p><table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse">
<tbody><tr style="vertical-align: top">
<td style="width: 48px; text-align: justify">&#160;</td>
<td style="width: 24px; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">b)</span></td>
<td style="text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">Change in accounts payable
    was $0.69 million net cash outflow for the year ended March 31, 2026. For the year ended March 31, 2025, the change in accounts payable
    was $0.11 million net cash outflow, which led to a $0.58 million increase in net cash outflow from operating activities.</span></td></tr>
</tbody></table><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&#160;</p><table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse">
<tbody><tr style="vertical-align: top">
<td style="width: 48px; text-align: justify">&#160;</td>
<td style="width: 24px; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">c)</span></td>
<td style="text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">Change in advance to suppliers
    was $0.55 million net cash outflow for the year ended March 31, 2026. For the year ended March 31, 2025, the change in advance to
    suppliers was $0.3 million net cash inflow, which led to a $0.25 million increase in net cash outflow from operating activities.</span></td></tr>
</tbody></table><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; text-align: left; margin-top: 0pt; margin-right: 0; margin-bottom: 0pt">&#160;</p><table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse">
